  "sources": [
    {"title": "E51C2, E51C3 Compact Bi-Directional Power and Energy Meter Installation Guide (Modbus Point Map)", "version": "ZL0067-0E (0818)", "date": "2018-08", "note": "Modbus point map, integer and floating point data; checked against the E51 Modbus Point Map 01111 (2011), which has the same registers"}
  ],
  "notes": [
    "Veris E51 (E51C2 full data set; E51C3 adds data logging).",
    "Power and energy are signed (import positive, export negative) where the manual says so; quadrant registers count reactive energy by quadrant.",
    "Addresses follow the manual's numbering, which starts at 1 (address_base 1). 32-bit values and floats have the most significant register first.",
    "Integer registers hold the value as an integer; the engineering value is the raw value times 10 to the power in the matching scale factor register (current, voltage, power, energy). Float registers need no scaling. Values the meter does not support in the chosen system type read as 0x8000 (integers) or NaN (floats).",
    "The meter answers on both FC03 and FC04; the map lists the registers as holding."
  ],
